			"id": "agent-analysis-harmony-entry-hap-form-and-liveform-provider",
			"interpretation": "products/phone is the entry HAP of a multi-module HarmonyOS sample. module.json5 declares EntryAbility, PhoneFormAbility (FormExtensionAbility), and a liveForm UIExtensionAbility; all ETS code delegates to sibling modules (@ohos/common, @ohos/abilitycommon, @ohos/commonbusiness, @ohos/widgetcommon), so its wiring (srcEntry paths, $profile/$string/$media references, onAddForm form names matching form_config.json, runtimeOnly packages) must stay in lockstep with them. Behavior: EntryAbility forwards lifecycle callbacks to BaseAbilityHelper; router_map builds MainPage (double-tap back-press to background, per-tab status-bar recoloring); main_pages registers SplashPage and live-form page Index, whose gyroscope parallax card reads rect/radius from LocalStorage and cancels overflow on click; PhoneFormAbility persists live-widget forms via FormRdbHelper and requests 3500 ms overflow animation. Contract: module.json5, form_config.json, router_map, main_pages, shortcuts_config, build-profile, and oh-package dependencies form one coupled unit; edits to sibling exports, form names, page paths, or permissions must be paired, which template tests do not catch.",
